<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Unicafe ups coffee figure to 23.1 mln bags.</title>
<headline>Brazil Unicafe ups coffee figure to 23.1 mln bags.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1997/98 coffee crop is now expected to reach 23.1 million 60-kg bags, up from a February forecast of between 19.7 million and 22.5 million 60-kg bags, according an estimate by leading exporter Unicafe.</p>
<p>The latest estimate published in local weekly &quot;Coffee Business&quot; plotted arabica production at 19.35 million bags and and conillon at 3.75 million bags.</p>
<p>In its first forecast in February, Unicafe had seen conillon production at between 3.9 million and 4.4 million bags and arabica at 15.8 million to 18.1 million bags.</p>
<p>A breakdown of Unicafe's estimate by state follows in millions of bags.</p>
<p> STATE			   2nd ESTIMATE	     1st ESTIMATE</p>
<p> Espirito Santo		  3.30			 3.40-3.80</p>
<p>    Arabica		    (1.00)		     (0.80-1.00)</p>
<p>    Conillon		   (2.30)		     (2.60-2.80)</p>
<p> Sao Paulo			 3.20			 2.70-3.00</p>
<p> Minas Gerais		   11.10			 8.80-9.90</p>
<p>    South			(6.00)		     (5.00-5.30)</p>
<p>    Cerrado		    (2.50)		     (2.00-2.30)</p>
<p>    Zona Da Mata	     (1.80)		     (1.50-1.80)</p>
<p>    Others			(0.80)		     (0.30-0.50)</p>
<p> Parana			    2.80			 2.50-2.80</p>
<p> Rondonia			  1.20			 1.00-1.20</p>
<p> Bahia			     1.00			 1.00-1.30</p>
<p> Others			    0.50			 0.30-0.50</p>
<p> TOTAL			    23.10			19.70-22.50</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
</text>
